# ── Secrets & environment files ─────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Node.js ────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# ── Python ─────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/

# ── Build output ────────────────────────────────────────
dist/
dist-ssr/

# ── Editor / OS files ───────────────────────────────────
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# ── Logs ────────────────────────────────────────────────
logs/
*.log

# ── The applications are versioned in their own repositories ────────────
# This repository tracks the project itself: the plan, the build board, the deployment notes and
# the one-command local launcher. The two applications under Backend/ and Frontend/ each carry
# their own git history and their own GitHub remote, so this one deliberately tracks neither --
# committing them here would put a second copy of the code on a second remote, and the two copies
# would drift the moment either app was pushed on its own.
#
# It also keeps the offline stores out for good. Backend/data holds real health data, profiles and
# the Memory Engine's personal facts, and the session store holds live tokens.
Backend/
Frontend/

# ── The workflow in this directory is a per-repo one ────────────────────
# .github/workflows/ci.yml here was written for a single checkout holding both applications side
# by side, which is not how this project is versioned. It cannot run in this repository and is
# not carried into either app, because each already has a workflow that passes on its own.
.github/
